    <h1>How Clients Book Appointments on Your Booking Page</h1>
    <p>The complete client booking experience — from selecting a service to receiving confirmation.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="blog-content">
    <p>One of the best things about Bookwize is how simple the booking process is for your clients. No app to download, no account to create — they just visit your booking link, choose what they need, pick a time, and confirm. Here is exactly what your clients see and do when they book an appointment.</p>

    <h2>The Booking Flow, Step by Step</h2>

    <div class="step-box">
      <h3>Step 1: Choose a Professional</h3>
      <p>When a client visits your booking page, they first see your team. Each <a href="/blog/managing-staff">staff member</a> is shown with their name and photo. Clients can pick the person they want, or choose <strong>"Any Available"</strong> to book the first open slot with whoever is free.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="step-box">
      <h3>Step 2: Select a Service</h3>
      <p>After choosing a professional, your client sees the list of <a href="/blog/adding-services">services</a> that person offers. Each service shows the name, duration, and price, so there are no surprises. If you have organized your services by category, clients can browse by group to find what they need quickly.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="step-box">
      <h3>Step 3: Pick a Date and Time</h3>
      <p>Next, clients see a <strong>calendar</strong> showing available dates. When they tap a date, the available <strong>time slots</strong> appear below. Only open times are shown — if a slot is already booked or falls outside your business hours, it does not appear. This means no double bookings and no confusion.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="step-box">
      <h3>Step 4: Enter Their Details</h3>
      <p>Your client enters their <strong>name</strong>, <strong>email address</strong>, <strong>phone number</strong>, and can add optional <strong>notes</strong> (like "running 5 minutes late" or "prefer the chair by the window"). That is all that is needed to complete the booking — no account creation required.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>After the Booking Is Confirmed</h2>
    <p>As soon as your client submits their booking, several things happen automatically:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Confirmation email</strong> — your client gets an immediate email with the appointment details: date, time, service, and staff member</li>
      <li><strong>Calendar invite</strong> — the confirmation includes a calendar file they can add to their phone or computer calendar with one tap</li>
      <li><strong>Manage link</strong> — the email includes a link to cancel or reschedule the appointment if their plans change</li>
      <li><strong>You get notified</strong> — you (and the assigned staff member) receive an email notification about the new booking</li>
    </ul>

    <blockquote>Your clients can book from any device — phone, tablet, or computer. No app download is needed. Just a web browser and your booking link.</blockquote>

    <h2>Cancelling or Rescheduling</h2>
    <p>Clients can cancel or reschedule through the manage link in their confirmation email. When they cancel, you and the assigned staff member are both notified automatically. The time slot becomes available again for other clients to book. You can also set a <a href="/blog/reducing-no-shows">cancellation policy</a> that requires a minimum notice period.</p>

    <h2>Works on Any Device</h2>
    <p>Your Bookwize booking page is fully responsive. Whether your client is on their phone waiting for coffee or on a laptop at home, the experience is smooth and easy to use. There is nothing to download, no login to create, and no friction that might stop them from completing the booking.</p>

    <div class="tip">
      <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Test the booking experience yourself. Visit your own booking page on your phone, walk through the steps as a client would, and make sure everything looks and feels right. You can always cancel the test booking afterward from your <a href="/blog/dashboard-guide">dashboard</a>.
    </div>

    <h2>Share Your Booking Link Everywhere</h2>
    <p>Your booking page link works anywhere you can share a URL. Put it on your Instagram bio, your Google Business profile, your Facebook page, or in your email signature. You can also <a href="/blog/embedding-widget">embed a booking widget</a> directly on your website so clients can book without leaving your site.</p>

